-# Working notes: 17b682bce66f
+# Review notes: 17b682bce66f, version 3.2.0
 
-Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
-Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+## D1 — finite-template concentration (reproduced and repaired)
+The incoming version has exactly 199 possible raw inputs and ten complete-scene
+translation classes. A 300-row seed prefix covers all normalized scenes in the
+next 300 rows in every band. Version 3.1.0 retained that bank as canonical/branch
+witnesses and added connected asymmetric rooted polyomino clouds plus independent
+legal source/anchor positions. The task-local census and exhaustive-capacity
+reports preserve the before/after evidence.
+
+## D2 — preserve the authority and exact witness predicates
+The rule writes each anchor in row-major order, then max-merges its paint. A
+later stamp may overwrite an earlier anchor, and a later anchor write may lower
+previous paint. Do not substitute an anchor-protected or commutative renderer.
+No Racket text, rule hash, approval ledger, or canonical signature changed.
+`strict_canonical_like` exposes the exact pre-existing canonical predicate; it
+does not relabel procedural examples as canonical.
+
+## D3 — procedural support remains deliberately bounded
+Keep the 8..16 canvas, 4/5-cell clouds within radius three, 4-connected
+source-plus-reference, asymmetric rotations, three/four distinct anchor colors,
+and full in-bounds stamps. There is no clipping, silent fixed-template fallback,
+or global RNG. A forced `scene_profile=procedural` seed/index is independent of
+difficulty; only the default mixture changes by band.
+
+## D4 — three visible examples previously left collision behavior open
+The version-3.1.0 public lesson probe found that broad geometric diversity alone
+did not guarantee a teaching window that distinguishes collision/order rules.
+The explicit competitor class in version 3.2.0 contains 119 alternatives:
+24 permutations of the color-to-quarter-turn map crossed with these policies:
+row-major max, reverse-order max, anchor-protected max, anchors-first max, and
+row-major overwrite; the intended map plus row-major max is omitted.
+
+Unforced draws use the schedule `contrastive, canonical, mixture`, repeated by
+`sample_index`. Every contiguous three-index window therefore has one procedural
+scene generated by bounded deterministic rejection until it disagrees with all
+119 alternatives, one exact canonical-profile draw, and one draw from the
+original band-specific mixture. The canonical role is deliberate: reserving one
+contrastive slot while leaving two ordinary mixture slots diluted pooled
+canonical-envelope support to 10/60 (16.7%) and failed the inherited 25% floor.
+The deterministic canonical role repairs that regression. Explicit profile
+overrides bypass the schedule, preserving the override contract.
+`lesson_identifiable` rejects a lesson only when a named competitor fits every
+demonstration and changes the query answer.
+
+## Evidence interpretation
+The task-local lesson probe compares the same declared competitor class across
+source versions. In the retained 300-lesson comparison, version 3.1.0 had 213/300
+query-identifiable windows and only 34/300 windows that refuted every competitor;
+version 3.2.0 had 300/300 for both measurements. The shared semantic gate also
+materialized Racket-authored outputs and accepted all 12 tested lessons across
+easy, medium, and hard. Real-authority parity is measured separately because the
+lesson probe deliberately uses the Python mirror for fast diagnostics.
+
+## Limitations
+The 119-member class is explicit and useful, but finite. Passing it is not a
+proof of universal rule identifiability, a Qwen improvement, masked solve
+correctness, or training suitability. Bounded procedural rejection can still
+raise loudly rather than silently substitute a template. The retained
+canonical-derived branch must not be treated as an independent held-out split.
